  "semantic_audit": [
    "Controller execs a separate supervisor for each side/repetition. Candidate code never runs in that supervisor: the native library is preloaded and each request handler executes only after fork. Child arenas and Unicorn machines are newly constructed; no child writes return to the parent memory image.",
    "ctypes parameters are explicit pointer/u32/restype declarations matching the extern C wrapper. Input bytes are copied into a 512-byte array; the full output array is returned. GuestMemory range construction, low-byte index, object bounds, narrow access widths, native function dispatch and mutant return hook match the legacy native adapter.",
    "Original preload checks independently read module bytes against fingerprint, PE32/x86 identity, registry module hash, unique file-backed slice range and original code hash. Code bytes are immutable; artifacts including binary are checked before/after comparison.",
    "Framing validates exact envelopes, request identities and counts, typed observations and complete process counts. Missing, duplicate, reordered, malformed, oversized and partial output cannot yield accepted complete reports. Exceptions, crashes, instruction budgets, watchdogs and nondeterminism fail acceptance.",
    "Start-gated fresh sessions publish active-case state before execution. Leaders remain unreaped until group cleanup; normal completion, case errors, supervisor crash and outer timeout are covered by real descendant regression tests.",
    "The paired freezer adds explicit runtime/wrapper/tests/coordinator review coverage and preserves public/heldout/negative stages. inspect_report verifies the precise newly built library, adapter, runtime, CMake inputs and full child counts before approval."
  ],
  "summary": "The exact frozen patch preserves the enumerated legacy observations and mandatory gates while moving each case into a fresh fork/session. No blocking soundness issue was found for the current allowlist."
